[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its reports hold more than one cause,
and the queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one bug. Fixing the parser leaves the booking-v3 date hint open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each cause now has its own ticket:

- `parser`: [issue #1](https://github.com/piotr921/mega-s01e03/issues/1)
- `hint`: [issue #2](https://github.com/piotr921/mega-s01e03/issues/2)

## What each cause is

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day
  first, so any date with a day up to 12 comes out with day and month swapped. This is the bug
  #4471 is named for.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
  first because the form tells them to, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. It
  happens only through the form, only at booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix does not touch it; the
  hint or the form's read order must change.

Some reports read as a one-day move, not a swap (`desk-notes.json`). The desk files them by tenant
and the table above counts them there, with a footnote. Check them again once the parser fix ships.

## How the reports are counted

- The export repeats some rows where its pages overlap: one id, one report (`uniqueById`).
- Each report is placed by its tenant's locale and booking form and its channel
  (`#lib/kb/causes.ts`), not by intake's tag. Intake tags follow the reporter's browser and
  disagree with the cause on both sides.
- Every number on this page comes from the desk's own components, computed from
  `reports-4471.json` at render time. When the desk adds reports, the page follows.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why they ended up in one ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Both causes
arrive under the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed up"), so subject matching
cannot keep them apart. Split by cause, as the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already does,
before marking a big ticket known.

